# Intent: Balance (spec docs/design/balance.md, rank 5 of docs/plan/more-games.md; input docs/design/accelerometer-games.md): a ball on a round plate rolls toward the lean of the unit (the analog reading of SF107, maipai_games_tilt_analog, roll and pitch in permille); the plate shrinks a pixel every two seconds and a hole opens every four after a warning ring; the ball off the plate or in a hole ends the game on Game over with the seconds (score-only, owner decision 33). Two new header-only files: the pure core (it takes the two lean values as arguments, so a host test drives it) with an autopilot and the dirty rectangles, and the screen (the plate, holes, ball and time chip in ONE draw callback, only what a tick changed invalidated). Registering the game, reading the lean, the 33 ms tick, the sounds (a soft rolling tick that rises toward the edge, thud, lose), the best score and the game-over call are the firmware track's.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_balance_core.h, maipai_balance.h (new, ours); reads maipai_games_tilt_analog (SF107)
# Check after a flash: Games, Balance: a ball on a blue plate; leaning the unit rolls it that way (small leans move it); a ring appears every four seconds and turns into a black hole a moment later; the plate shrinks; the ball off the plate or in a hole ends on Game over with the seconds; flat on the desk the ball does not move and the plate shrinks past it within two minutes.
# Kconfig: none

diff --git a/firmware/main/hal/maipai_balance_core.h b/firmware/main/hal/maipai_balance_core.h
